/-!
# An affine local domain model of a missing image point

Source: Stacks Project, Tag 0CM2, `limits-lemma-reach-point-closure-Noetherian`,
first paragraph of proof, expanded in affine coordinates using Algebra Tags
00CO, 00CT, 00FN and 07BH (blueprint: lem-sfb-boundary-affine-local-domain-model).
-/

@[expose] public section

universe u

open CategoryTheory

namespace AlgebraicGeometry

/-- A boundary point of the image of a finite-type morphism has an affine model
whose localized prime quotient is a nonfield Noetherian local domain inside the
residue field of a source point. The maps `a` and `hbar` are fixed by their
compatibility equations; `e` presents `R` as the prescribed prime localization.
The three field equivalences are canonical by their compatibility on generators.

Source: Stacks Project, Tag 0CM2, first paragraph of proof, expanded using Algebra
Tags 00CO, 00CT, 00FN and 07BH.
(blueprint: lem-sfb-boundary-affine-local-domain-model)

Proof:
1. Finite type includes quasi-compactness (def-weil-finite-type-morphism).
   Apply lem-sc-picard-closure-specialization to obtain x with g(x) specializing
   to y; it differs from y since y is outside the image. Choose a Noetherian
   affine neighbourhood V of y (pqf-def-locnoeth). It contains g(x), since opens
   contain every generalization of their points. Choose an affine W inside its
   inverse image containing x, with finite-type coordinate map by
   def-weil-finite-type-morphism.
2. Under these charts, lem-weil-pbc-spec-map-residue-field-naturality identifies
   the prime of g(x) as q = phi inverse image of r. In a spectrum, specialization
   is inclusion of primes (def-weil-affine-spectrum). Distinctness gives q < p.
3. By lem-weil-pbc-prime-residue-field-algebra, h = B -> C -> kappa(r) has kernel
   q. It induces an injection hbar of A = B/q into L. Thus A is a nonzero domain;
   P = p/q is a proper prime, nonzero since q < p. Set R = A_P.
4. Send a/s to hbar(a)/hbar(s). The denominators are nonzero. Equality of
   fractions, by def-weil-pbc-localization-at-prime, reduces in the domain A
   to cross multiplication, so this is a ring map. Its zero kernel follows
   from injectivity of hbar; it factors h and makes R a nonzero domain.
5. The fractions whose numerators lie in P form PR. Fractions with numerator
   outside P are units, by reversing them; those with numerator in P cannot
   be units, since cross multiplication would put a product of denominators
   in P. Thus PR is the unique maximal ideal; its contraction in B is p.
   A nonzero element of P remains nonzero in R and is a nonunit, so R is not
   a field (def-weil-pbc-localization-at-prime).
6. Finite generators descend to ideals of B/q. An ideal in its localization
   is generated by images of generators of its contraction, since a/s in an
   ideal implies a/1 is in that ideal. This proves Noetherianity from
   def-weil-pbc-noetherian-ring.
7. The quotients of elements of R in L form a subfield. Each quotient
   (a/s)/(b/t) is at/(sb), and every quotient of elements of A is a quotient
   of elements of R. Thus this is both Frac(A) and Frac(R). By
   lem-weil-pbc-prime-residue-field-algebra it is also kappa(q); the maps
   agree with h on B, which determines the field identifications uniquely.
-/
theorem exists_boundary_affine_local_domain_model
    {U Y : Scheme.{u}} (g : U ⟶ Y) [LocallyOfFiniteType g] [QuasiCompact g]
    [IsLocallyNoetherian Y] (y : Y)
    (hy : y ∈ closure (Set.range g) \ Set.range g) :
    ∃ (x : U) (V : Y.Opens) (W : U.Opens)
      (B C : CommRingCat.{u}) (v : Spec B ≅ V.toScheme) (w : Spec C ≅ W.toScheme)
      (φ : B →+* C),
      y ∈ V ∧ x ∈ W ∧ W ≤ g ⁻¹ᵁ V ∧
      w.hom ≫ W.ι ≫ g = Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom φ) ≫ v.hom ≫ V.ι ∧
      φ.FiniteType ∧ IsNoetherianRing B ∧ g x ⤳ y ∧ g x ≠ y ∧
      ∃ (p q : PrimeSpectrum B) (r : PrimeSpectrum C),
        V.ι (v.hom p) = y ∧ W.ι (w.hom r) = x ∧
        V.ι (v.hom q) = g x ∧ q.asIdeal = r.asIdeal.comap φ ∧
        q.asIdeal < p.asIdeal ∧
        ∃ (P : PrimeSpectrum (B ⧸ q.asIdeal)),
          P.asIdeal = p.asIdeal.map (Ideal.Quotient.mk q.asIdeal) ∧
          RingHom.ker ((algebraMap C r.asIdeal.ResidueField).comp φ) = q.asIdeal ∧
          ∃ (R : CommRingCat.{u}) (e : R ≃+* Localization.AtPrime P.asIdeal)
            (a : B →+* R) (hbar : (B ⧸ q.asIdeal) →+* r.asIdeal.ResidueField)
            (ι : R →+* r.asIdeal.ResidueField) (hlocal : IsLocalRing R),
            e.toRingHom.comp a =
              (algebraMap (B ⧸ q.asIdeal) (Localization.AtPrime P.asIdeal)).comp
                (Ideal.Quotient.mk q.asIdeal) ∧
            hbar.comp (Ideal.Quotient.mk q.asIdeal) =
              (algebraMap C r.asIdeal.ResidueField).comp φ ∧
            Function.Injective ι ∧
            ι.comp a = (algebraMap C r.asIdeal.ResidueField).comp φ ∧
            (∀ (b : B ⧸ q.asIdeal) (s : P.asIdeal.primeCompl),
              ι (e.symm (IsLocalization.mk' (Localization.AtPrime P.asIdeal) b s)) =
                hbar b / hbar s) ∧
            IsNoetherianRing R ∧ IsDomain R ∧ ¬ IsField R ∧
            @IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal R _ hlocal =
              (P.asIdeal.map (algebraMap (B ⧸ q.asIdeal)
                (Localization.AtPrime P.asIdeal))).map e.symm.toRingHom ∧
            Ideal.comap a (@IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal R _ hlocal) = p.asIdeal ∧
            ∃ (K : Subfield r.asIdeal.ResidueField),
              (∀ t : r.asIdeal.ResidueField,
                t ∈ K ↔ ∃ b c : R, c ≠ 0 ∧ t = ι b / ι c) ∧
              (∃ eA : FractionRing (B ⧸ q.asIdeal) ≃+* K,
                ∀ b : B,
                  (eA (algebraMap (B ⧸ q.asIdeal) (FractionRing (B ⧸ q.asIdeal))
                    (Ideal.Quotient.mk q.asIdeal b)) : r.asIdeal.ResidueField) =
                    algebraMap C r.asIdeal.ResidueField (φ b)) ∧
              (∃ eκ : q.asIdeal.ResidueField ≃+* K,
                ∀ b : B, (eκ (algebraMap B q.asIdeal.ResidueField b) :
                  r.asIdeal.ResidueField) = algebraMap C r.asIdeal.ResidueField (φ b)) ∧
              (∃ eR : FractionRing R ≃+* K,
                ∀ b : R, (eR (algebraMap R (FractionRing R) b) :
                  r.asIdeal.ResidueField) = ι b) := by
  sorry

end AlgebraicGeometry
